## External Backlinks and Referrals

Sharepanel.host’s online presence is primarily noted in community forums and review sites. Key referring domains and backlink examples include:

- **reddit.com (r/SharePanelHost, r/SharepanelAffiliated, r/selfhosted):** Multiple threads on Reddit discuss SharePanel and link to `sharepanel.host` or its subdomains. The anchor text is typically the raw URL (e.g. “https://sharepanel.host”). Reddit is a high-traffic community forum (high domain authority), so these links are seen as user-generated endorsements. For instance, users on r/SharepanelAffiliated have shared links and reviews of sharepanel.host (anchor text = URL).  *(Trust: Reddit is widely used and generally considered authoritative for user discussions.)*

- **scamadviser.com:** Scamadviser is an automated review site that lists sharepanel domains. It provides a “Visit site” link (anchor text “sharepanel.host”) and rates sharepanel.host with a “slightly low trust score” ([sharepanel.host Reviews | check if site is scam or legit| Scamadviser](https://www.scamadviser.com/check-website/sharepanel.host#:~:text=sharepanel,Why)). It similarly lists **mta.sharepanel.host** with a “very low trust score” (warns it “may be a scam”) ([mta.sharepanel.host Reviews | scam, legit or safe check | Scamadviser](https://www.scamadviser.com/check-website/mta.sharepanel.host#:~:text=mta,Why)). These are algorithmic assessments, so the anchor text is the URL itself (“sharepanel.host” and “mta.sharepanel.host”) but trust is flagged as low by the site’s criteria.

- **linkedin.com:** The founder’s LinkedIn profile (Maliq Barnard/Sahwe) links to `sharepanel.host` and mentions it in context. (E.g. the LinkedIn summary includes “sharepanel.host” and links to it.) Anchor text is the URL or project name. LinkedIn is high-authority for personal profiles (link trust high), but this is user-authored content.

- **Other forums/blogs:** Aside from Reddit, there are few to no major tech media backlinks. A handful of personal or niche posts mention SharePanel (e.g. an Italian self-hosting community post praises the site by its URL). In general, there are no prominent tech publications linking to SharePanel. The referring domains are mostly community sites and review aggregators. 

In summary, the backlink profile is limited: mostly from user forums (anchor text usually the raw URL “sharepanel.host”) and one review site. Scamadviser’s links (with low trust scores) are the most notable, but no high-authority tech or news sites are known to link to sharepanel.host.

